      "independent_reference": {
        "source": "Ballistic kinematic limit of differentiable MLS-MPM: a single particle with F=I, C=0 has zero neo-Hookean stress and zero APIC first moment (Sum w*dpos == 0 for the quadratic B-spline), so the APIC round-trip degenerates to PIC free-flight x(T)=x0+dt*Sum v_t with dx(T)/dv0=dt*STEPS*I; the one-target L2 loss gives dLoss/dv0 = 2(dt*STEPS)^2 (v0 - v0_target), EXACT. Hand-derived kinematics; DiffTaichi (Hu et al., ICLR 2020, arXiv:1910.00935) is the differentiable-MPM method citation.",
        "derived_by": "closed-form-analytic (ballistic kinematics)",
